00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.380
So can you kind of lay out the landscape for
us a little bit?

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:45.380
Sure.

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:49.200
The political movements are pretty complicated.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:52.629
And this one is, I think, more complex than
most.

00:00:52.629 --> 00:00:53.950
Most it's kind of centralists.

00:00:53.950 --> 00:01:00.340
It consists of a variety of for profit and
nonprofit organizations, legal advocacy groups,

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:07.010
right wing policy groups, data initiatives,
media and messaging workshops, legislative

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:08.010
initiatives.

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:13.060
So, you know, the movement's leaders, are
there a number of them?

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:16.340
They're often interconnected through some
of these initiatives.

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:22.099
But it's it's a really vast kind of movement
with a lot of different components.

00:01:22.099 --> 00:01:28.579
And it shows the extent to which this the
Christian right has organized over decades,

00:01:28.579 --> 00:01:31.310
really, in building this kind of infrastructure.

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:36.779
Can you give a couple of the examples that
might be more surprising to people of where

00:01:36.779 --> 00:01:39.100
what what some of the components are?

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:40.100
Sure.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:45.499
I mean, let's start with the legislative initiative
called Project Blitz.

00:01:45.499 --> 00:01:49.259
It operates a little bit like the American
Legislative Exchange Council.

00:01:49.259 --> 00:01:50.399
You know what that is?

00:01:50.399 --> 00:01:54.319
They craft centrally craft legislation.

00:01:54.319 --> 00:02:00.219
And then these different pieces of identical
or near identical legislation are they flood

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:05.529
the states, all of them, and intending to
sort of chip away bit by bit at the separation

00:02:05.529 --> 00:02:08.209
of church and state in different ways.

00:02:08.209 --> 00:02:16.290
So, for instance, this past year and a half
